    (v_topic_id, 'A 72-year-old postmenopausal woman is prescribed oral alendronate 70 mg weekly for newly diagnosed osteoporosis. Which of the following instructions regarding proper administration is most important to ensure adequate drug absorption and minimize the risk of adverse effects?', '["Take the tablet first thing in the morning on an empty stomach with a full glass (6-8 oz) of plain water; remain upright (sitting or standing) for at least 30 minutes before eating, drinking anything else, or taking other medications, to prevent esophageal irritation and ensure absorption", "Take the tablet at bedtime with a glass of milk to enhance calcium-mediated absorption and reduce gastrointestinal upset", "Take the tablet with coffee or orange juice because acidic beverages enhance bisphosphonate bioavailability", "Take the tablet with food to minimize the risk of nausea; lying down immediately after ingestion is acceptable", "Take the tablet at any time of day with any beverage; the timing and food intake do not affect absorption or safety"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Oral bisphosphonates have extremely **low bioavailability (< 1%)**. To maximize absorption and minimize esophageal adverse effects, patients must: (1) Take the tablet **first thing in the morning on an empty stomach** (fasting), (2) Swallow with a **full glass (6-8 oz) of plain water only** (no coffee, juice, milk, or mineral water, as calcium, magnesium, iron, and other minerals chelate bisphosphonates and prevent absorption), (3) **Remain upright (sitting or standing) for at least 30 minutes** (60 minutes for ibandronate) to prevent esophageal irritation, ulceration, and stricture, and (4) **Wait at least 30 minutes before eating, drinking, or taking other medications**. Non-adherence to these instructions is the most common cause of treatment failure and esophageal complications. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 77; First Aid Step 2 CK; AGS Geriatrics At Your Fingertips)'),
